<!--
  The official TMDB logo, converted from the SVG published at
  https://www.themoviedb.org/about/logos-attribution (the "blue_long_1" asset) into an Android
  vector drawable. Required by TMDB's API terms, which #137 quotes in full.

  DO NOT EDIT THE PATH OR THE GRADIENT. TMDB's branding rules are explicit: "Our logo should not be
  modified in color, aspect ratio, flipped or rotated." The path data below is theirs, byte for
  byte, and the three gradient stops are their published colours. The declared width and height are
  the SVG's own 423.04 x 35.4 viewport scaled uniformly, so the ratio is preserved; that is the part
  the rule cares about. A caller needing a different size must scale both axes together (Compose's
  ContentScale.Fit does), never one.

  Re-deriving this file: fetch the asset above and copy its single <path d="..."> across. It is one
  path with one userSpaceOnUse linear gradient, which is why the conversion is lossless.

  BUT DO NOT COPY THE PATH DATA UNCHANGED. One transformation is required, and skipping it produces
  a logo that looks right everywhere except on an actual phone.

  Their path is many subpaths, and seven of them open with a relative "m" straight after a "Z". Per
  the SVG spec, the point after a closepath is the START of the subpath just closed, so the move is
  measured from there. Android's PathParser measures it from the last point drawn instead, so those
  seven land in the wrong place: on an SM-G975U1 the wordmark read "THE M-V = DB", with the I gone,
  the E collapsed to an equals sign and the D carrying an artifact.

  Every subpath start here has therefore been rewritten as an absolute "M" with the coordinate the
  spec says it resolves to. That is a re-spelling, not an edit: the geometry is theirs, unchanged,
  which is what their no-modification rule is about. Three of the rewritten starts can be checked
  against the absolute coordinate their own subpath closes back onto - 296.3, 351.29 and 204.06 -
  and they agree.

  Skia follows the spec, so Roborazzi renders the BROKEN version correctly and the golden cannot
  see this. TmdbLogoDrawableTest asserts the property on this file instead. If it fails, redo the
  absolute conversion; do not delete the test.
-->
